  "reading": {
    "id": "n4.l04.r01",
    "lessonId": "n4.l04",
    "title": "理想のアパート探しの条件 (Conditions for Finding an Ideal Apartment)",
    "level": "N4",
    "text": "日本で留学生や社会人がアパートを探すとき、何を重視すればよいでしょうか。多くの人は家賃、駅からの距離、部屋の広さなどを条件に挙げます。\n\n一般的に、駅から近ければ近いほど通勤や通学には便利ですが、その分家賃も高くなります。家賃が安ければ生活費を節約できますが、駅から歩いて二十分以上かかると、雨の日や夜遅い帰宅のときに大変です。\n\nまた、部屋は広ければ広いほど荷物をたくさん置けて快適ですが、冬は暖房が効きにくく、電気代も高くなりがちです。不動産屋に行ってよく相談すれば、自分の予算や生活スタイルに合った物件を提案してもらえます。焦って決めずに、いくつかの部屋を実際に見学して比べれば、後悔しない部屋探しができるはずです。",
    "kanaText": "日本で留学生や社会人がアパートを探すとき、何を重視すればよいでしょうか。多くの人は家賃、駅からの距離、部屋の広さなどを条件に挙げます。\n\n一般的に、駅から近ければ近いほど通勤や通学には便利ですが、その分家賃も高くなります。家賃が安ければ生活費を節約できますが、駅から歩いて二十分以上かかると、雨の日や夜遅い帰宅のときに大変です。\n\nまた、部屋は広ければ広いほど荷物をたくさん置けて快適ですが、冬は暖房が効きにくく、電気代も高くなりがちです。不動産屋に行ってよく相談すれば、自分の予算や生活スタイルに合った物件を提案してもらえます。焦って決めずに、いくつかの部屋を実際に見学して比べれば、後悔しない部屋探しができるはずです。",
    "translation": "When international students and working adults look for an apartment in Japan, what should they prioritize? Many people list conditions such as rent, distance from the station, and room size.\n\nGenerally, the closer it is to the station, the more convenient commuting to work or school becomes, but rent becomes higher accordingly. If rent is cheap, one can save on living expenses, but if it takes over 20 minutes to walk from the station, it is tough on rainy days or when returning late at night.\n\nAlso, the more spacious a room is, the more belongings one can place and the more comfortable it is, but heating takes longer in winter, and electricity bills tend to rise. If you go to a real estate agency and consult carefully, they will propose properties matching your budget and lifestyle. Rather than rushing, if you visit several rooms in person and compare them, you should be able to find a room without regrets.",
    "questionIds": [
      "n4.l04.q021",
      "n4.l04.q022",
      "n4.l04.q023",
      "n4.l04.q024",
      "n4.l04.q025"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "glossary": [],
    "prov": {
      "source": "Nihongo N2 Master Editorial Team (Native Review)",
      "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
      "rev": 2
    },
    "titleMy": "理想のアパート探しの条件 (Conditions for Finding an Ideal Apartment) (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "理想のアパート探しの条件 (Conditions for Finding an Ideal Apartment) (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "When international students and working adults look for an apartment in Japan, what should they prioritize? Many people list conditions such as rent, distance from the station, and room size.\n\nGenerally, the closer it is to the station, the more convenient commuting to work or school becomes, but rent becomes higher accordingly. If rent is cheap, one can save on living expenses, but if it takes over 20 minutes to walk from the station, it is tough on rainy days or when returning late at night.\n\nAlso, the more spacious a room is, the more belongings one can place and the more comfortable it is, but heating takes longer in winter, and electricity bills tend to rise. If you go to a real estate agency and consult carefully, they will propose properties matching your budget and lifestyle. Rather than rushing, if you visit several rooms in person and compare them, you should be able to find a room without regrets."
  },
