  "grammars": [
    {
      "id": "n4.l13.g001",
      "lessonId": "n4.l13",
      "pattern": "[Subject] は [Agent] に [Verb 使役受身形 (〜させられる / 〜される)]",
      "meaning": "Causative-Passive (being forced/made to do an action against one's will or with reluctance)",
      "formation": "Group 1: a-row + される (contracted): 待つ -> 待たされる, 行く -> 行かされる, 飲む -> 飲まされる. Note: verbs ending in す use させられる (話す -> 話させられる).\nGroup 2: ru -> させられる (食べる -> 食べさせられる, 覚える -> 覚えさせられる)\nGroup 3: 来る -> こさせられる, する -> させられる",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "The causative-passive (使役受け身) indicates that the subject was made or pressured by someone else (marked by に) to perform an action that they found burdensome, exhausting, or didn't originally want to do.",
