    "titleMy": "部活動の合宿と成長の思い出 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "部活動の合宿と成長の思い出 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "In the summer of my first year in high school, I participated in the soccer club's summer training camp. It was far stricter than normal practices, leaving me with many unforgettable memories even today.\n\nDuring camp, we were woken abruptly at 5:30 every morning and made to run a 5-kilometer mountain road as a whole squad before breakfast. Being poor at running, my legs hurt and I felt like stopping many times, but cheered on loudly by seniors, I managed to finish running. Furthermore, after afternoon practice, all first-years were made to stay late weeding the athletic field and polishing soccer balls.\n\nAt that time, I felt dissatisfied, wondering: \"Why are we made to do only such painful chores?\" However, when camp ended and we returned to school, I noticed that my stamina had improved drastically compared to before. Furthermore, our bonds with classmates who overcame the hard training together had deepened.\n\nBack then I felt like I was being forced against my will, but looking back now, I appreciate it as a valuable experience that cultivated my endurance."
