    "titleMy": "日本企業におけるお客様の迎え方 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "日本企業におけるお客様の迎え方 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "In Japanese companies, when welcoming guests from outside the firm, great attention is paid to language choice and etiquette. In order to demonstrate respect to the counterparty, it is required to properly use \"keigo,\" particularly \"sonkeigo\" (respectful speech), which differs from daily casual conversations.\n\nWhen a guest arrives at the reception desk, staff greet them first with a smile: \"Welcome. We have been expecting you.\" Then, after confirming their name and purpose of visit, they courteously guide them: \"I will guide you to the reception room. Please proceed this way.\"\n\nAfter escorting them into the reception room, the guest is invited to sit in the seat of honor (\"kamiza\") on the sofa. When serving green tea, one says \"Please enjoy the tea.\" Furthermore, while waiting for the person in charge to arrive, to prevent the guest from becoming bored, it is also important to suggest: \"Would you please take a look at this new product document while waiting?\"\n\nUsing respectful language properly is not only a sign of respect toward the other party, but an essential business manner that elevates the company's credibility."
