    },
    "titleMy": "週末の旅行計画と台風の進路 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "週末の旅行計画と台風の進路 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "This weekend, four university friends and I have planned a 2-day, 1-night trip to a hot spring inn in Nagano Prefecture. We booked the inn a month ago, secured reserved seats on the limited express train, and looked forward to the trip as preparations progressed.\n\nHowever, watching last night's weather forecast, it was reported that a large typhoon formed over southern waters and could potentially approach the Kanto through Koshin regions over the weekend. If it continues on this course, we might be struck by heavy rain and gale winds on Saturday afternoon, and express trains might be suspended.\n\nWe hurriedly consulted via a group call. Our friend Nakamura said: \"The path might still change, so let's wait until tomorrow.\" On the other hand, Tanaka-san worried: \"Mountain roads carry landslide risks, so if we force ourselves to go, we might not be able to return home from the inn.\"\n\nChecking the railway company's website, it stated: \"Weekend train operation plans will be announced at 5:00 PM on Friday.\" Checking the forecast and latest updates, they should make a decision prioritizing safety above all. Although it was a trip we all anticipated, we agreed to act prudently without taking reckless risks."
