    "titleMy": "ユニバーサルデザインと使いやすさの追求 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "ユニバーサルデザインと使いやすさの追求 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "In recent home appliances and daily goods, the concept of \"Universal Design\" is being widely adopted. This design philosophy aims to create products that are \"easy to use and hard to mistake\" for everyone, regardless of age, nationality, or physical disability.\n\nConventional home appliances had problems where functions increased too much, creating too many buttons, or manual text was too fine and hard to read. Especially for elderly people unfamiliar with operating machinery, settings were too complicated and difficult to master.\n\nHowever, modern microwave ovens and washing machines have simplified operation panels, adopting large, easy-to-see fonts and voice guidance. Furthermore, various safety enhancements are incorporated, such as using plastic materials that are hard to crack even if dropped, or attaching handles that are non-slip even with wet hands.\n\nWhen products become excessively convenient, they can paradoxically become harder to use. Products that are intuitive and easy to handle for anyone truly enrich people's lives."
