    "titleMy": "電子書籍と紙の本の未来 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "電子書籍と紙の本の未来 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "In recent years, along with the spread of smartphones and dedicated e-readers, readers who use electronic books are rapidly increasing. E-books have many merits, such as being able to carry hundreds of books inside a single light device and freely altering font sizes.\n\nHowever, physical paper books will likely never disappear completely. In fact, according to a questionnaire survey of book lovers, people who answer \"I love the feeling of turning physical pages and the smell of books\" or \"Looking at books lined up on a bookshelf gives me peace of mind\" still constitute the majority. Moreover, opinions remain firmly rooted that paper books are easier to handle for grasping the overall structure and quickly flipping back to re-read previous pages.\n\nIn short, aren't e-books and paper books partners that should be used distinctively according to the situation, rather than enemies competing over superiority? For example, reading lightweight, convenient e-books on commuter trains or travels, while opening paper books when leisurely enjoying reading at home on weekends. Such a reading style should truly enrich our intellectual lives the most."
