      "source": "Nihongo N2 Master Editorial Team (Native Review)",
      "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
      "rev": 2
    },
    "titleMy": "町で話題の新しいベーカリー (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "町で話題の新しいベーカリー (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "Recently, a rumor has been spreading through the shopping district in front of the station where I live. In the location that was an old stationery shop until a few months ago, a new handmade bakery is apparently opening next week.\n\nAccording to neighborhood talk, the owner-baker is apparently a skilled artisan who trained in France for many years. Freshly baked croissants and natural yeast baguettes in particular are said to be exquisite, already gaining popularity with orders coming in from surrounding cafes.\n\nYesterday evening when I walked past the shop, through the window glass I could see the interior renovations were mostly finished. With a calm wood-grain design, it radiated a warm atmosphere truly characteristic of a small European town bakery.\n\nOn opening day, specially made rusks will apparently be handed out to the first fifty customers. For me, who loves delicious bread, I can hardly wait for the opening. Next Saturday, I think I will wake up early and line up."
