  "reading": {
    "id": "n4.l25.r01",
    "lessonId": "n4.l25",
    "title": "週末旅行の行き先相談",
    "level": "N4",
    "text": "秋の連休に日本のどこかへ一泊二日で旅行したいと考えているなら、まず何を一番楽しみたいかを決めることが大切です。\n\nもし美味しい郷土料理と温泉で心身を癒やしたいなら、群馬県の草津温泉や神奈川県の箱根温泉がおすすめです。東京からのアクセスも良く、古い歴史を持つ旅館に泊まれば、日常の疲れを忘れてのんびり過ごすことができます。\n\n一方、秋ならではの自然や鮮やかな紅葉の景色を満喫したいなら、栃木県の日光や山梨県の富士五湖周辺が最適です。山沿いの道を歩くと、赤や黄色に染まった木々が湖に映り、息をのむほど美しい光景に出会えます。\n\nただし、秋の観光地は大変混雑するため、泊まりたい宿が決まったなら、なるべく早く予約を完了させましょう。",
    "kanaText": "あきのれんきゅうににほんのどこかへいっぱくふつかでりょこうしたいとかんがえているなら、まずなにをいちばんたのしみたいかをきめることがたいせつです。\n\nもしおいしいきょうどりょうりとおんせんでしんしんをいやしたいなら、ぐんまけんのくさつおんせんやかながわけんのはこねおんせんがおすすめです。とうきょうからのアクセスもよく、ふるいれきしをもつりょかんにとまれば、にちじょうのつかれをわすれてのんびりすごすことができます。\n\nいっぽう、あきならではのしぜんやあざやかなこうようのけしきをまんきつしたいなら、とちぎけんのにっこうややまなしけんのふじごこしゅうへんがさいてきです。やまぞいのみちをあるくと、あかやきいろにそまったきぎがみずうみにうつり、いきをのむほどうつくしいこうけいにであえます。\n\nただし、あきのかんこうちはたいへんこんざつするため、とまりたいやどがきまったなら、なるべくはやくよやくをかんりょうさせましょう。",
    "translation": "If you are thinking of traveling somewhere in Japan for a two-day one-night trip during the autumn consecutive holidays, it is important to first decide what you want to enjoy most.\n\nIf you want to heal body and mind with delicious local cuisine and hot springs, Kusatsu Onsen in Gunma or Hakone Onsen in Kanagawa is recommended. Access from Tokyo is good, and if you stay at an inn with long history, you can forget daily fatigue and spend time leisurely.\n\nOn the other hand, if you want to fully enjoy nature unique to autumn and vivid autumn foliage scenery, Nikko in Tochigi or around the Fuji Five Lakes in Yamanashi is ideal. Walking along mountain paths, trees dyed red and yellow reflect in the lakes, creating breathtakingly beautiful views.\n\nHowever, since autumn sightseeing spots get extremely crowded, if the inn you wish to stay at has been decided, let's complete the reservation as early as possible.",
    "questionIds": [
      "n4.l25.q025",
      "n4.l25.q026",
      "n4.l25.q027"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "glossary": [],
    "prov": {
      "source": "Nihongo N2 Master Editorial Team (Native Review)",
      "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
      "rev": 2
    },
    "titleMy": "週末旅行の行き先相談 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "titleMyanmar": "週末旅行の行き先相談 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "If you are thinking of traveling somewhere in Japan for a two-day one-night trip during the autumn consecutive holidays, it is important to first decide what you want to enjoy most.\n\nIf you want to heal body and mind with delicious local cuisine and hot springs, Kusatsu Onsen in Gunma or Hakone Onsen in Kanagawa is recommended. Access from Tokyo is good, and if you stay at an inn with long history, you can forget daily fatigue and spend time leisurely.\n\nOn the other hand, if you want to fully enjoy nature unique to autumn and vivid autumn foliage scenery, Nikko in Tochigi or around the Fuji Five Lakes in Yamanashi is ideal. Walking along mountain paths, trees dyed red and yellow reflect in the lakes, creating breathtakingly beautiful views.\n\nHowever, since autumn sightseeing spots get extremely crowded, if the inn you wish to stay at has been decided, let's complete the reservation as early as possible."
