    "titleMyanmar": "海外旅行前の持ち物確認と準備 (ဖတ်ရှုခြင်း)",
    "translationMy": "When embarking on an overseas trip for the first time, anyone feels great anxiety alongside anticipation. So that you won't be troubled after arriving at the airport, it is important to carefully create a checklist one week before departure and confirm whether or not all necessary preparations are in order.\n\nFirst, you must verify whether or not your passport's expiration date has ample validity of 6 months or more remaining. Furthermore, you also need to check in advance on the embassy's official website whether or not a visa is required to enter the destination country.\n\nNext, information regarding money and communications—such as whether smartphones can be used locally or where currency exchange fees are cheapest—is also vital. Confirming beforehand with your credit card company whether or not your card is configured for overseas use brings peace of mind.\n\nNobody can predict what might happen at the travel destination. However, if you carefully verify one by one in advance what is necessary, you can greatly reduce the likelihood of encountering trouble."
