      "pattern": "[Verb Dictionary / ている / た-form] + ところだ",
      "meaning": "Temporal point: about to do / in the middle of doing / have just finished doing",
      "formation": "[Verb 辞書形] + ところだ (Imminent: about to do)\n[Verb ている] + ところだ (In progress: currently doing)\n[Verb た形] + ところだ (Immediate completion: just finished seconds/moments ago)",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "ところ indicates an exact temporal stage along the timeline of an action:\n1. 辞書形＋ところ: 0% completion — right on the brink of commencing (often with これから / ちょうど).\n2. ている＋ところ: 50% in progress — captured midway through the continuous process (often with 今 / ちょうど).\n3. た形＋ところ: 100% finished — fresh footprint of literal immediate termination (often with たった今 / さっき).\nImportant Restriction: 〜たところ indicates objective seconds or minutes ago. It CANNOT be used with distant past markers like 先週 or 去年.",
