    {
      "id": "n5.l30.g001",
      "lessonId": "n5.l30",
      "pattern": "Verb Form Integration (て形・ない形・た形・辞書形)",
      "meaning": "Mastery and systematic synthesis of the 4 core verb conjugations",
      "formation": "Dictionary Form (食べる) / て-form (食べて) / ない-form (食べない) / た-form (食べた)",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "The 4 fundamental verb forms unlocked all N5 grammar patterns:\n1. て-form: Requests (〜てください), Continuous (〜ています), Permission (〜てもいい), Connecting (〜てから).\n2. ない-form: Negative request (〜ないでください), Obligation (〜なければなりません).\n3. た-form: Experience (〜たことがある), Non-exhaustive listing (〜たり〜たり), Advice (〜たほうがいい), Conditional (〜たら).\n4. Dictionary form: Ability (〜ことができる), Hobby (〜ことです), Before (〜前に), Natural condition (〜と).",
        "my": "ဂျပန်ဘာသာ အခြေခံ ကြိယာ ၄ မျိုး (Dictionary-form, て-form, ない-form, た-form) သည် N5 သဒ္ဒါပုံစံအားလုံး၏ အဓိက မဏ္ဍိုင်ဖြစ်သည်။ ၎င်းတို့ကို စနစ်တကျ ပြန်လည်ပေါင်းစပ်လေ့ကျင့်သည်။"
      },
      "examples": [
        {
          "sentenceId": "n5.l30.s001",
          "note": "Conjugation review"
        },
        {
          "sentenceId": "n5.l30.s004",
          "note": "Multiple forms in context"
        }
      ],
      "similarGrammarIds": [],
      "commonMistakes": [
        "Pay special attention to Group 1 consonant-stem verbs (e.g. 書く → 書いて/書かない/書いた; 泳ぐ → 泳いで/泳がない/泳いだ; 待つ → 待って/待たない/待った)."
      ],
      "difficulty": 1,
      "level": "N5",
